        "id": 255709,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-12-06T15:44:59.078Z",
        "cooked": "<p>To address the overall topic, the idea was basically a reason to have Sentinels characters acting out non-Sentinels stories, and it was a pretty creative framing on the whole.</p>\n<p>The “European Fairy Tales” part was for copyright reasons, which is not particularly surprising as C&amp;A are as bound to that as their fictional metaverse is. I can’t fault them for that part.</p>\n<p>I agree that the reveal of him as a frustrated writer was a little underwhelming, but that doesn’t make the overall idea any less fun for me.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"skywhale\" data-post=\"20\" data-topic=\"30354\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/skywhale/48/5248_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> skywhale:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There have been recent additions that I don’t particularly like, but I like that they added because it’s more similar to real-world comic books (the werewolves and demon twins, for example). They certainly did start with the more popular stuff in EE</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The irony is the recent things you list are <em>also</em> popular. The werewolves and Soul Twins have been crazy popular in this RL fandom.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2023-12-06T15:48:37.195Z",
